            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>Disclosed is a composition for conferring durable water repellence to woven or non-woven fabric, comprising (a) an aqueous solvent comprising at least 80 w/w% water, and 20 w/w% or less of a water miscible organic solvent comprising at least two functional OH groups, (b) 0.1 - 40 w/w% of an acrylic ester having the formula 1:wherein A&amp;lt;sup&amp;gt;1&amp;lt;/sup&amp;gt; is H or CH&amp;lt;sub&amp;gt;3&amp;lt;/sub&amp;gt;, and A&amp;lt;sup&amp;gt;2&amp;lt;/sup&amp;gt; is C&amp;lt;sub&amp;gt;1&amp;lt;/sub&amp;gt;-C&amp;lt;sub&amp;gt;30&amp;lt;/sub&amp;gt; linear or branched, saturated or unsaturated hydrocarbon that may have an alicyclic or aromatic ring, the acrylic ester being dissolved, emulsified or dispersed in the aqueous solvent, and (c) a polyisocyanate comprising at least 3 crosslinkable isocyanate groups. Further disclosed is a method for conferring durable water repellence to woven or non-woven fabric, comprising the steps of (1) treating the fabric the aqueous composition, and (2) heating the treated fabric to 120 - 200°C. Further, a fabric treated with such a composition are disclosed.</p>
            </abstract>
